\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A MoSES (Mobile Stasis Energy System) drone was not, by itself, especially impressive. It was roughly the size of a suitcase, though less useful for carrying socks, and had the blunt, over-engineered appearance of something designed by people who distrusted both beauty and warranty claims. Its shell was a dull composite wrapped around lift rotors, attitude jets, sensors and enough processing hardware to keep track of several hundred other MoSES drones simultaneously without once asking where everybody was going.\
At its centre sat a Gyges disc.\
The disc was mounted in a compact articulated cradle that allowed it to spin, tilt and alter its orientation while the drone itself moved independently around it. Fridge Force had taken considerable care to ensure that no operator could casually get at the disc, partly because Gyges components were expensive and partly because generations of technicians had demonstrated that a warning label reading DO NOT OPEN tended to function mainly as an invitation to apprentices.\
A single drone could generate little of practical use. MoSES became interesting in company.\
Once several drones entered the same operational volume, they began arranging themselves relative to one another. They did not fly in formation so much as continuously negotiate one. Distances changed by centimetres, then metres. One drone climbed while another dropped. Arcs tightened into rings, rings stretched into ellipses, and apparently disordered swarms resolved for fractions of a second into geometries whose significance was obvious only to the machines and a small number of Fridge Force physicists who had long ago stopped being invited to normal parties.\
The geometry mattered. So did the relative phase of the discs, their orientation and the degree to which the array held coherence.\
Change those relationships and the stasis field changed with them.\
A wide configuration could suspend a broad volume. A tighter arrangement could narrow the effect around a person, a vehicle or a particular piece of machinery. Shift the drones again and the active field could move without any of the drones going especially near whatever was being inconvenienced.\
